--Description:
--Step 1: pick a publication number that demonstrably appears inside at least one "citation"
--        array anywhere in the database (so we know it is being cited).  
--Step 2: search the PUBLICATIONS table for every record whose own "citation" array contains
--        that sampled publication number.  
--The query therefore always returns rows and lets us observe the reverse‑citation pattern
--(who cites whom).  Showing the first 20 citing publications is enough to verify structure.
