Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "publication_number": unique identifier of each patent publication – needed to identify the patent that might be cited and to look it up in other records.  
• "grant_date": numeric YYYYMMDD – used to keep only patents that were actually granted in the calendar‑year 2010.  
• "application_kind": high‑level patent type – filter to utility patents (value usually ‘A’; if your data uses ‘U’ for utility‑model patents, test both).  
• "filing_date": numeric YYYYMMDD – provides the start‑date from which the 10‑year forward‑citation window is measured.  
• "application_number": identifier of the citing publication – will be counted DISTINCT to know how many separate forward citations a patent received.  
• "citation": VARIANT (JSON array) that lists the publications a given patent cites.  By scanning this array we can find which later publications reference (i.e., cite forward to) an earlier publication.  
• "publication_date": numeric YYYYMMDD – can be used when you want to be sure the citing publication was published inside the forward‑citation window as a further refinement (optional).  

Typical conditions you are likely to combine  
• t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231  
• t."application_kind" = 'A'      -- or test for 'U' as well, depending on how your dataset codes utility patents  
• REGEXP_LIKE(f.value:"publication_number"::STRING, target_pub_no_regex)  
• c."filing_date" <= t."filing_date" + 100000   -- crude 10‑year window (YYYYMMDD + 100000 ≈ +10 years)  
• HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT c."application_number") = 1  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that move from very simple inspection through to a full query structure able to return the requested count.  Adjust database / schema / table names if they differ, always enclosing identifiers in double‑quotes.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Peek at a few 2010‑granted publications to view core columns.
SELECT
  "publication_number",
  "grant_date",
  "filing_date",
  "application_kind"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Check which distinct "application_kind" values appear in 2010 grants.
SELECT DISTINCT
  "application_kind"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Inspect the raw JSON in the "citation" column for one sample 2010 patent.
SELECT
  "publication_number",
  "citation"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
  AND "citation" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Flatten the "citation" array for that single sample to see its structure.
SELECT
  t."publication_number"            AS "citing_pub",
  f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE t."publication_number" = '<REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE_PUB>'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Look up who cites a specific publication number (reverse‑search).
-- Replace '<TARGET_PUB>' with an actual publication number obtained above.
SELECT
  c."publication_number"   AS "citing_pub",
  c."application_number"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."citation") f
WHERE f.value:"publication_number"::STRING = '<TARGET_PUB>'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: List every pair (early_pub, later_pub) where later_pub cites early_pub,
-- restricted to early_pub granted in 2010 and later_pub filed within 10 years of early_pub.
WITH early AS (
  SELECT "publication_number", "filing_date"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
    AND "application_kind" = 'A'
)
SELECT
  e."publication_number"         AS "early_pub",
  c."publication_number"         AS "later_pub",
  c."application_number"         AS "later_app_no"
FROM early e
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."citation") f
       ON f.value:"publication_number"::STRING = e."publication_number"
WHERE c."filing_date" BETWEEN e."filing_date" AND (e."filing_date" + 100000)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Count DISTINCT citing application numbers per 2010‑granted utility patent.
WITH early AS (
  SELECT "publication_number", "filing_date"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
    AND "application_kind" = 'A'
)
SELECT
  e."publication_number",
  COUNT(DISTINCT c."application_number") AS "forward_cite_cnt"
FROM early e
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."citation") f
       ON f.value:"publication_number"::STRING = e."publication_number"
WHERE c."filing_date" BETWEEN e."filing_date" AND (e."filing_date" + 100000)
GROUP BY e."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Keep only those early patents that have EXACTLY one forward citation.
WITH early AS (
  SELECT "publication_number", "filing_date"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
    AND "application_kind" = 'A'
),
forward_ct AS (
  SELECT
    e."publication_number"              AS "early_pub",
    COUNT(DISTINCT c."application_number") AS "forward_cite_cnt"
  FROM early e
  JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c
       , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."citation") f
         ON f.value:"publication_number"::STRING = e."publication_number"
  WHERE c."filing_date" BETWEEN e."filing_date" AND (e."filing_date" + 100000)
  GROUP BY e."publication_number"
)
SELECT *
FROM forward_ct
WHERE "forward_cite_cnt" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Compute the TOTAL number of 2010‑granted utility patents
-- that have exactly one forward citation inside the 10‑year window.
WITH early AS (
  SELECT "publication_number", "filing_date"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
    AND "application_kind" = 'A'
),
forward_ct AS (
  SELECT
    e."publication_number",
    COUNT(DISTINCT c."application_number") AS "forward_cite_cnt"
  FROM early e
  JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c
       , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."citation") f
         ON f.value:"publication_number"::STRING = e."publication_number"
  WHERE c."filing_date" BETWEEN e."filing_date" AND (e."filing_date" + 100000)
  GROUP BY e."publication_number"
)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "num_utility_pats_with_one_forward_cite"
FROM forward_ct
WHERE "forward_cite_cnt" = 1;
```

```sql
--10) Description: Same as Query 9 but also returns the publication numbers for manual auditing.
WITH early AS (
  SELECT "publication_number", "filing_date"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20101231
    AND "application_kind" = 'A'
),
forward_ct AS (
  SELECT
    e."publication_number",
    COUNT(DISTINCT c."application_number") AS "forward_cite_cnt"
  FROM early e
  JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c
       , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."citation") f
         ON f.value:"publication_number"::STRING = e."publication_number"
  WHERE c."filing_date" BETWEEN e."filing_date" AND (e."filing_date" + 100000)
  GROUP BY e."publication_number"
)
SELECT
  "publication_number",
  "forward_cite_cnt"
FROM forward_ct
WHERE "forward_cite_cnt" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

